Chloe / Vivek — adding a few tactical notes we should share in the doc bundle and on the call:

SDK and compatibility
- Confirmed: redwood-inference==2.1.0 is the minimal GA we support for the cutover. The change set includes automatic Retry-After parsing and jittered backoff helper (client.retry.with_jitter()).
- If NovaCorp uses an older homegrown client, include a simple edge proxy to translate the headers and add an Authorization header. This is lower risk than changing many clients in one go.

Endpoint migration matrix (excerpt)
old: https://api.novacorp.com/v1/gen -> new: https://api.redwood.com/v1/generate
- Header mapping: X-Client-Id -> x-nc-client-id (lowercase enforced by proxy)
- Streaming: you must keep Transfer-Encoding: chunked for the streaming route; do not set a Content-Length on those requests.

Retries/timeouts (practical snippet)
- Pseudocode (JS):

async function callWithBackoff(fn, attempts = 3) {
  let base = 200;
  for (let i=0; i<attempts; i++) {
    try {
      return await fn();
    } catch (err) {
      if (err.status === 429) {
        const retryAfter = err.headers['retry-after'];
        const wait = retryAfter ? parseInt(retryAfter) * 1000 : (base * Math.pow(2, i));
        await sleep(wait + jitter());
      } else if (err.status >= 500) {
        await sleep(base * Math.pow(2, i));
      } else {
        throw err;
      }
    }
  }
  throw new Error('exhausted retries');
}

Rate-limit bump and monitoring
- Vivek, can you provision a temporary +30% ingress quota on June 8 02:00-06:00 UTC? We'll monitor token-level error rates and abort if error rate > 1%.
- We'll add a lightweight health-check route that validates 200 within 3s for each stage.

I'll draft the implementation checklist and post it to the Drive folder referenced below.

